WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:02.140
So this is a program

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:03.900
that is motivated and
driven

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:05.240
by a really long-term vision

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:07.259
to understand

00:00:07.259 --> 00:00:08.800
the fundamental building blocks

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.360
of matter
and how we behave.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:20.830
This is one of these driving questions of humanity
that we want to understand how our world works,

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:23.460
that we want to understand where we are coming
from.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.840
We have gathered a team,

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.020
and this team is
very international.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.180
So it's across different continents

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.060
and I challenge you to find

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:33.420
a funding scheme which

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.920
allows you to do this like CIFAR

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:37.520
really for
them it's not a problem.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:39.860
On the contrary for them

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:41.170
it's even an asset
yeah.

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:47.070
And we saw that this is really a very complex
project that the 2 of us could not master

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:51.720
ourselves, and then the most natural thing
that came to our mind is CIFAR.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:53.080
CIFAR can do this.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:56.740
CIFAR connect fast, it can enable collaborations.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:01:00.920
Also CIFAR has a track record of enabling collaborations
very efficiently.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:07.900
CIFAR can do this fast, and also it can glue
these participants together and into one program

00:01:07.909 --> 00:01:09.799
and hold an organization together.

00:01:09.799 --> 00:01:15.510
And of course this in turn later on will also
have impact on the other disciplines as these

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:23.850
techniques and [INAUDIBLE] develop will later
on have impact on [INAUDIBLE] material science,

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:24.880
[INAUDIBLE].

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:30.159
And this is strongly related to questions
such as what happened during the big bang?

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:33.620
Why is there more matter than anti-matter?

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:35.160
So why are we here actually?

00:01:35.179 --> 00:01:39.690
What is the nature of dark matter that we
observe in the universe?

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:44.960
And how actually these processes of these
particles, these fundamental building blocks

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:46.420
how this takes place.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:53.260
[Music]

